            <ArticleTitle>Endoscopic retrieval of toothbrushes in a schizophrenic patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>63-64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Foreign bodies are a common problem in the daily endoscopic practice. Nevertheless, long objects as toothbrushes, sometimes pose a special problem when trying to remove them from the stomach, due to the difficulty of passing through the hiatus. Endoscopic retrieval of toothbrushes has seldom be reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
